    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "Done. The feature is implemented and the full suite is green (263 tests, `BUILD SUCCESS`).\n\n## What I changed\n\n`POST /api/owners` now supports an optional `Idempotency-Key` header. A repeat create with an already-seen key returns the originally created owner with **200**, instead of creating a duplicate (which the identity-uniqueness rule would reject with 409).\n\n**New function classes** (`rest/function/owner/`):\n- `IdempotencyKeyRegistry` \u2014 a `@Component` singleton mapping seen key \u2192 created owner id (lives outside the request transaction, so a key stays \"seen\").\n- `CheckIdempotencyKey` \u2014 new entry step. Reads the header via `@HttpHeaderParameter(\"Idempotency-Key\")` (injects `null` when absent). Takes exactly one of two `@Flow` branches: `replay` (key seen and owner still exists) or `create` (normal pipeline).\n- `ReplayFlow` / `CreateFlow` \u2014 the two `@Flow` functional interfaces.\n- `RespondWithExistingOwner` \u2014 responds 200 with the original owner (mirrors `RespondWithOwner`'s body).\n- `RecordIdempotencyKey` \u2014 after `SaveOwner` (id assigned), records the key; no-op when no header.\n\n**`owners.POST.yml`** \u2014 prepended `checkIdempotency` (entry, `outputs: {replay, create}`, no `next`), added `respondExisting`, and inserted `recordIdempotency` between `save` and `audit`.\n\n## Key design note\n\nI verified against the OfficeFloor sources that a step's `next:` **always fires** regardless of return value, so a `next` + called `@Flow` would run *both* paths. The correct either/or is an entry step with **only** `outputs:` (no `next`) that always calls exactly one flow \u2014 which is why the existing linear create chain is now reached via the `create` flow rather than being the HTTP entry. All 30 existing owner tests (400/409 validation and duplicate paths) still pass, confirming escalations propagate correctly through the flow.",
