    "probe_text": "I now have the complete pipeline. Here is the full, ordered account.\n\n## `POST /api/owners` \u2014 validations and side-effects, in order\n\nEverything below runs inside **one transaction** (`govern: [ transaction ]` on every step), so it commits once at the end and any thrown escalation rolls the whole thing back.\n\n### 0. Gate (before any step)\n- **Authorization**: `authorize: \"hasRole('OWNER_ADMIN')\"` \u2014 caller lacking that role is rejected (403 via `AuthorizationDeniedException` handler).\n\n### 1. `CheckIdempotencyKey` \u2014 idempotent-create branch\n- Reads the `Idempotency-Key` header. If present, non-blank, previously recorded, and the recorded owner still exists **and is not soft-deleted** \u2192 takes the **replay** branch:\n  - **`RespondWithExistingOwner`**: returns the original owner as `OwnerDto` (with `bulkSignupWarning` set) at **200 OK**. No new owner is persisted. *(Pipeline ends here.)*\n- Otherwise (no key, unseen key, or original owner gone/deleted) \u2192 **create** branch into the steps below.\n\n### 2. `ValidateOwner` (validation) \u2014 *only step binding `@RequestBody`*\n- `@Valid` bean validation on `OwnerFieldsDto` (schema constraints).\n- Additionally rejects (400 `MethodArgumentNotValidException`) when missing **or blank**:\n  - `firstName`, `lastName`, `city`, `telephone`.\n  - address: rejects only if **both** normalized `addressLine1` and normalized flat `address` are blank (either form satisfies it).\n- Publishes the validated DTO as a variable for later steps.\n\n### 3. `ValidatePostcode` (validation)\n- Only if `postcode` is present. Must match `[0-9]{4}`.\n- If `city` maps to a known region (Sydney\u2192NSW, Melbourne\u2192VIC, Brisbane\u2192QLD), postcode must fall in that region's inclusive range (NSW 2000\u20132099, VIC 3000\u20133099, QLD 4000\u20134099). Otherwise 400. Unknown city \u2192 any 4-digit postcode accepted.\n\n### 4. `NormalizeOwnerTelephone` (validation + mutation)\n- Converts `telephone` to canonical E.164; strips spaces/dashes/brackets; assumes `+61` and drops a single leading `0` when no country code given.\n- Requires 8\u201315 digits after `+`; with an explicit country code, enforces national length (`+61`\u21929, `+1`\u219210). Invalid \u2192 400.\n- **Side-effect**: writes the E.164 value back onto the request.\n\n### 5. `NormalizeOwnerEmail` (validation + mutation)\n- Only if `email` is non-null. Must be syntactically valid \u2192 else 400.\n- Rejects known disposable domains (`mailinator.com`, `tempmail.com`, `guerrillamail.com`) \u2192 400.\n- **Side-effect**: lower-cases the email and writes it back.\n\n### 6. `NormalizeOwnerAddress` (mutation)\n- If structured `addressLine1` present: normalizes `addressLine1`/`addressLine2` (trim, collapse whitespace, upper-case, expand ST\u2192STREET, RD\u2192ROAD, AVE\u2192AVENUE) and recomposes the flat `address`. Else normalizes only the flat `address`.\n\n### 7. `EnsureOwnerCityCapacity` (validation)\n- Counts existing owners in the same city (case-insensitive). If \u2265 **50** \u2192 **409** `CityAtCapacityException`.\n\n### 8. `NormalizeRegistrationDate` (validation + derives value)\n- Supplied date later than today \u2192 **400** (`FutureDate`). Effective date = supplied, else today.\n- Rolls the date forward past Saturdays, Sundays, and listed 2026 public holidays to the next business day.\n- Publishes the adjusted date as a variable (used by the daily-limit, build, and membership-number steps).\n\n### 9. `EnsureDailyOwnerLimit` (validation)\n- Counts existing owners whose `registrationDate` equals the adjusted date. If \u2265 the daily limit \u2192 **429** `DailyOwnerLimitException`.\n\n### 10. `BuildOwner` (constructs entity)\n- Maps the DTO to an `Owner` (via `OwnerMapper`) and sets its `registrationDate` to the adjusted business day. Published as the `Owner` variable that all following steps mutate in place.\n\n### 11. `AssignCustomerCode` (mutation)\n- Sets `customerCode = \"<REGION>-<HASH8>\"`: region from postcode (else city, else `UNKNOWN`); HASH8 = first 8 upper-hex of SHA-256 over `telephone + lastName`.\n- De-duplicates against existing codes by appending `-2`, `-3`, \u2026 as needed.\n\n### 12. `AssignHouseholdId` (mutation)\n- If postcode present: `householdId` = first 12 hex of SHA-256 over `normalizedLastName + \"|\" + postcode`. No postcode \u2192 left null.\n\n### 13. `EnsureHouseholdUnique` (validation)\n- If `sharesHousehold` is true, or no `householdId` \u2192 skip.\n- Else if any non-deleted existing owner has the same `householdId` \u2192 **409** `DuplicateHouseholdException`.\n\n### 14. `EnsureOwnerIdentityUnique` (validation)\n- If any non-deleted existing owner has the same `identityKey` (`telephone|email|householdId`) \u2192 **409** `DuplicateIdentityException`.\n\n### 15. `AssignHouseholdSize` (mutation)\n- Sets `householdSize` = count of owners sharing this `householdId` including the new one (1 if no household). Snapshot taken pre-save.\n\n### 16. `AssignNamesakeCount` (mutation)\n- Sets `namesakeCount` = existing owners with the same first+last name (case-insensitive), excluding self. Pre-save snapshot.\n\n### 17. `AssignPossibleDuplicate` (mutation)\n- Declared household member (`sharesHousehold`) \u2192 `possibleDuplicate=false`, `possibleDuplicateOf=null`.\n- Else if a non-deleted owner shares last name + postcode but has a **different** telephone \u2192 `possibleDuplicate=true`, `possibleDuplicateOf` = lowest matching id; otherwise false/null.\n\n### 18. `AssignMembershipLevel` (mutation)\n- Computes `membershipPoints` (0 base; +2 email present; +1 if `namesakeCount==0`; +2 if `householdSize\u22653`; +3 if >1 fiscal year tenure) and maps to `membershipLevel` (1\u20134). Stores both.\n\n### 19. `AssignMembershipNumber` (mutation)\n- Sets `membershipNumber = \"<customerCode>-M<YY>\"`, YY = last two digits of the fiscal year (starts 1 July) of the registration date.\n\n### 20. `SaveOwner` (persistence side-effect)\n- `ownerRepository.save(owner)` \u2014 persists the row and assigns the id.\n\n### 21. `RecordIdempotencyKey` (side-effect)\n- If the request carried a non-blank `Idempotency-Key`, records `key \u2192 owner.id` in the singleton registry (first-write-wins, lives outside the transaction). No-op otherwise.\n\n### 22. `AuditOwnerCreated` (side-effect)\n- Logs an `AUDIT` line: owner id, customerCode, registrationDate, membershipLevel, membershipNumber.\n\n### 23. `RespondWithOwnerCreated` (response side-effect)\n- Maps to `OwnerDto`, sets `bulkSignupWarning` (`OwnerBulkSignup.isWarning`), responds **201 Created** with `Location: /api/owners/{id}`.\n\n---\n\n**Notes:** Validations 2\u20135, 8 return **400**; capacity/duplicate conflicts (7, 13, 14) return **409**; daily limit (9) returns **429**. Any `DataIntegrityViolationException` at save has its own escalation handler, and anything unmatched falls to the `java.lang.Exception` handler."
